   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## Result for $[3,1,0]$ (15 states, point with $\\chi_3=7/2$)\n- **Quantum determinant.** $t^G_3=\\chi_3\\nu_1(u)\\nu_2(u-h)\\nu_3(u-2h)$ holds exactly, symbolically.\n- **Direct equation.** $Q_i=z_i^{-x/h}q_i$ with $\\deg q_i=\\lambda_1-\\mu_i$ for all 15 states.\n- **Dual equation.** $Q^j=z_j^{+x/h}q^j$ with $\\deg q^j=\\mu_j$ for all 15 states.\n- **Control.** The wrong-sign asymptotics give no polynomial solutions.\n- **QQ relation.** $Q_a(u)Q_b(u+h)-Q_b(u)Q_a(u+h)=(1/z_b-1/z_a)(u-\\theta+2h)(u-\\theta+3h)Q^c(u)$ for all states and all cyclic $(a,b;c)$, with residual 0. This confirms $F_\\lambda=\\prod_{n=\\lambda_2+1}^{\\lambda_1}(u-\\theta+nh)$.\n- **Wronskians.** The formulas for $t_{1,2,3}$ are exact.\n- **The Casoratian.** $D_{1,0,-1}$ has roots at $x-\\theta=-3,-2,-1,0$, and for the adjoint they were $-2,-1,0$. Both fit $D_{1,0,-1}\\propto\\prod_{n=0}^{\\lambda_1}(x-\\theta+nh)$, but both reps have $\\lambda_3=0$ and $|\\mu|=\\lambda_1+1$. A rep such as $[3,2,0]$ or $[4,1,0]$ would separate this from other guesses.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## Functional orthogonality from adjointness (L=1)\n**Notation.** $O$ is the direct operator, which acts on $Q_i$. $O^\\dagger$ is the dual operator in uniform form, which acts on $P=Q^j$:\n$$O^\\dagger P=\\nu_3(x)\\nu_3(x-h)\\nu_3(x-2h)P(x+h)-t_1(x)\\nu_3(x-h)\\nu_3(x-2h)P(x)+t_2(x)\\nu_3(x-2h)P(x-h)-t_3(x)P(x-2h).$$\nTake the bracket $\\langle F\\rangle$ to be the sum of residues of $\\mu F$ over **all** poles of the rational measure $\\mu$. The $Q$'s are polynomials times exponentials, which are entire, so this is invariant under $x\\to x-kh$ term by term.\n\n**Adjointness.** Shifting each term turns $\\langle\\mu\\,P\\,O[Q]\\rangle$ into $\\langle\\mu\\varphi\\,O^\\dagger[P]\\,Q\\rangle$, provided\n$$\\varphi=\\frac{\\nu_1(x+h)\\nu_1(x+2h)}{\\nu_3(x-h)\\nu_3(x-2h)},\\qquad\\frac{\\mu(x+h)}{\\mu(x)}=\\frac{\\nu_3(x)}{\\nu_1(x+3h)}\\;\\Rightarrow\\;\\mu=\\prod_{n=\\lambda_3}^{\\lambda_1+2}\\frac1{x-\\theta+nh}.$$\nAll four terms give consistent conditions.\n\n**Orthogonality.**\n- **What is left.** $O_BQ_B=0$ and $O^\\dagger_AP_A=0$, so only $\\delta t_a=t_a^B-t_a^A$ survives. Here $\\delta t_1=\\delta I_1$ is a constant, $\\delta t_2$ is linear, and $t_3$ is the same for every state.\n- **Splitting $\\delta t_2$.** Write $\\delta t_2(y)=a\\,\\nu_1(y)+b\\,\\nu_3(y-h)$, with the $a$ part in direct form and the $b$ part shifted to dual form. Every term then has the measure $\\rho=\\mu\\nu_1(x+h)\\nu_1(x+2h)=\\prod_{n=\\lambda_3}^{\\lambda_1}(x-\\theta+nh)^{-1}$.\n- **The relation.** For every pair $(i,j)$,\n$$-\\delta I_1\\langle Q^j_AQ_{i,B}\\rangle_\\rho+a\\langle Q^j_AQ^{[2]}_{i,B}\\rangle_\\rho+b\\langle Q^{j[-2]}_AQ_{i,B}\\rangle_\\rho=0,\\qquad\\langle f\\rangle_\\rho=\\sum_{n=\\lambda_3}^{\\lambda_1}\\frac{f(\\theta-nh)}{\\prod_{m\\ne n}(m-n)h}.$$\n  So for $A\\neq B$ every $3\\times3$ determinant $\\det N^{AB}$ of these row vectors vanishes.\n\nThis is the old $\\{-Q^jQ_i,\\,Q^jQ_i^{[-2]},\\,Q^{j[2]}Q_i\\}$ under $h\\to-h$, with the poles moving from $\\theta+nh$ to $\\theta-nh$.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* full Q's at h=1: Q_i = z_i^(-x) q_i (direct), Q^j = z_j^(+x) q^j (dual) *)\ngbQD[A_, i_, x_] := N[gbZ[[i]]^(-x), gbPrec] (gbQd[[A, i]] /. X -> x);\ngbQU[A_, j_, x_] := N[gbZ[[j]]^x, gbPrec] (gbQu[[A, j]] /. X -> x);\ngbPoles = Range[gbLam[[3]], gbLam[[1]]];\ngbW[n_] := 1/Product[(m - n) (h /. gbPt), {m, DeleteCases[gbPoles, n]}];\ngbRow[A_, B_, {i_, j_}] := Sum[With[{x = (θ[1] /. gbPt) - n}, gbW[n] {-gbQU[A, j, x] gbQD[B, i, x], gbQU[A, j, x] gbQD[B, i, x + 1], gbQU[A, j, x - 1] gbQD[B, i, x]}], {n, gbPoles}];\ngbPairs = Tuples[Range[3], 2];\ngbNs = Length[gbVal];\n(* sanity: δt1 constant and δt2 linear for every pair of states, so exactly three unknowns *)\ngbDtOK = And @@ Flatten[Table[{Exponent[Chop[Expand[gbVal[[A, 1]] - gbVal[[B, 1]]], 10^-30], u] <= 0, Exponent[Chop[Expand[gbVal[[A, 2]] - gbVal[[B, 2]]], 10^-30], u] <= 1, Chop[Expand[gbVal[[A, 3]] - gbVal[[B, 3]]], 10^-30] === 0}, {A, gbNs}, {B, gbNs}]];\ngbNmat = Table[gbRow[A, B, #] & /@ gbPairs, {A, gbNs}, {B, gbNs}];\n(* for each of the 84 row triples: max |det| over A != B relative to min |det| over A = B *)\ngbTriples = Subsets[Range[9], {3}];\ngbTripleStats = Table[With[{d = Table[Det[gbNmat[[A, B]][[tr]]], {A, gbNs}, {B, gbNs}]},\n    {gbPairs[[tr]], Min[Abs[Diagonal[d]]], Max[Abs[Flatten[d - DiagonalMatrix[Diagonal[d]]]]]}], {tr, gbTriples}];\n(* also the rank statement directly: smallest singular value of the 9x3 matrix, A != B vs A = B *)\ngbSV = Table[Min[SingularValueList[N[gbNmat[[A, B]], 30], Tolerance -> 0]], {A, gbNs}, {B, gbNs}];\ngbGood = Select[gbTripleStats, #[[2]] > 10^-20 &];\ngbOrthRes = <|\"rep\" -> gbLam, \"states\" -> gbNs, \"3 unknowns\" -> gbDtOK,\n   \"max offdiag / min diag over all triples nonzero on diag\" -> N[Max[#[[3]]/#[[2]] & /@ gbGood], 3],\n   \"# triples nonzero for every A=B\" -> Length[gbGood],\n   \"min sv A=B\" -> N[Min[Diagonal[gbSV]], 3], \"max sv A!=B\" -> N[Max[Flatten[gbSV - DiagonalMatrix[Diagonal[gbSV]]]], 3]|>;\nIf[! AssociationQ[gbOrthAll], gbOrthAll = <||>]; gbOrthAll[gbLam] = gbOrthRes;\nToString[gbOrthRes, InputForm]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
