   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "**Result: functional orthogonality at L=1** (point with $\\chi_3=7/2$; reps $[2,1,0]$, $[3,1,0]$, $[3,2,0]$, $[2,1,1]$).\n\nFor every rep:\n- **Three unknowns.** $\\delta t_1$ is constant, $\\delta t_2$ is linear and $\\delta t_3=0$.\n- **Rank.** For $A\\neq B$ the $9\\times3$ matrix $\\big(-\\langle Q^jQ_i\\rangle_\\rho,\\ \\langle Q^jQ_i^{[2]}\\rangle_\\rho,\\ \\langle Q^{j[-2]}Q_i\\rangle_\\rho\\big)_{(i,j)}$ has rank 2, with smallest singular value $\\lesssim10^{-39}$, against $\\gtrsim1$ for $A=B$.\n- **Determinants.** Every $3\\times3$ $\\det N^{AB}$ that is nonzero on the diagonal satisfies $\\det N^{AB}\\propto\\delta_{AB}$, with ratio $\\lesssim10^{-45}$.\n- **Row choices.** 77 of the 84 choices of three rows work. The 7 that fail all have the same $i$, all the same $j$, or are $\\{(1,1),(2,2),(3,3)\\}$. The old choice $\\{(1,3),(1,2),(2,3)\\}$ and its mirror $\\{(3,1),(2,1),(3,2)\\}$ both work.\n- **Measure.** $\\rho=\\prod_{n=\\lambda_3}^{\\lambda_1}(x-\\theta+nh)^{-1}$, with poles at $\\theta-nh$. This was confirmed at $\\lambda_3=1$.\n\n**Correction found at $[2,1,1]$.** The dual degree is $\\deg q^j=\\mu_j-\\lambda_3$, not $\\mu_j$; the two agree when $\\lambda_3=0$. The direct degree $\\lambda_1-\\mu_i$ is unchanged. The QQ relation with $F_\\lambda=\\prod_{n=\\lambda_2+1}^{\\lambda_1}(u-\\theta+nh)$ and the Wronskian formulas for $t_{1,2,3}$ hold for all four reps.\n\n**Open.**\n- **The Casoratian.** Its roots in $x-\\theta$ are $\\{0,-1,-2\\}$ for $[2,1,0]$, $\\{0,\\dots,-3\\}$ for $[3,1,0]$, $\\{0,-1,-1,-2,-3\\}$ for $[3,2,0]$ and $\\{-2\\}$ for $[2,1,1]$. So the earlier guess $\\prod_{n=0}^{\\lambda_1}$ is wrong; the degree is $|\\lambda|-3\\lambda_3$.\n- **Normalization.** The relation between $\\det N^{AA}$ and $\\langle\\Psi_A|\\Psi_A\\rangle$ in the new conventions, i.e. the analogues of $\\Psi^{\\rm ref}$, $c^{\\rm ref}$ and $\\kappa$ in the old notebook.\n\nThe kernel currently holds `gbLam = {2,1,1}`; the cell outputs above are for that rep.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  }
 ],
